# `A⁻¹ @ b` with a PositiveDefinite `A` is rewritten to a Cholesky solve;
# `inv(A) @ b` is the same operator spelled as a call. The explanation
# names the operands by their source text.
# env: A: Matrix[N,N] PositiveDefinite
# env: b: Vector[3]
# env: K: Matrix[3,3] PositiveDefinite
# env: f: Vector[3]
x = A⁻¹ @ b
y = inv(A) @ b
u = K⁻¹ @ f
w = inv(K⁻¹) @ (f + f)
